course: dictionary
lesson: 374
title: Antlers: branched bony horns
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An antler is one of the two branched, bony horns on the head of a deer, elk, moose or reindeer. The branches look a bit like the twigs on a tree.
explain: Read the clues around the word: «Antlers fall off and grow again every year, unlike horns, which stay for life.» The words "unlike horns" tell you that antlers are different. A horn stays on for life, but an antler drops off and grows back.
explain: Male deer use antlers to fight other males in the mating season. While new antlers grow, they are covered in soft, furry skin called velvet.
fact: An antler is a branched, bony horn on the head of a deer, elk, moose or reindeer.
fact: Antlers fall off and grow again every year. Horns stay on for life.
fact: The tips of an antler are called points or tines.
fact: Reindeer are the only deer where both males and females grow antlers.
exercise: What is an antler? | A kind of fish that lives in rivers | *A branched, bony horn on a deer's head | A soft, furry blanket for a deer
exercise: «Antlers fall off and grow again every year, unlike horns, which stay for life.» Which word tells you antlers are different from horns? | stay | grow | every | *unlike
exercise: «Each tip of an antler is called a point or tine.» What are the tips of an antler called? | Hooves | Lichen | *Points or tines | Velvet
test: Which animals can have antlers? | Only birds and fish | *Deer, elk, moose and reindeer | Only cats and dogs
test: What is special about reindeer among deer? | Reindeer have no horns at all | Reindeer never grow antlers | *Both males and females grow antlers
exam: Which fact about antlers is true? | Antlers stay on for life | *Antlers fall off and grow again every year | Antlers are soft, furry skin all the time | Antlers grow only on fish
